{
  "case_id": "2018-17-1484",
  "document_hash": "f2c87647294b01e39896ea21e7ce25cdf4078b9f3e1e030772acc2f4712804b3",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Edwin S. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1484",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2c87647294b01e39896ea21e7ce25cdf4078b9f3e1e030772acc2f4712804b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2c87647294b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 1395hh did not require CMS to go through notice-and-comment rulemaking before it could furnish its calculation of one component of a hospital's reimbursement to the contractors that perform the initial determination of reimbursement for the agency. That calculation was not binding on the agency, the courts, or Respondents, and it could be challenged on administrative appeal, as, in fact, Respondents did here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1484",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2c87647294b01e39896ea21e7ce25cdf4078b9f3e1e030772acc2f4712804b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2c87647294b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is -- is this right? I mean, I -- it's very complicated, what you're saying. I thought it was quite simple, that for a long time in Medicare they didn't have to follow the APA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Edwin S. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1484",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2c87647294b01e39896ea21e7ce25cdf4078b9f3e1e030772acc2f4712804b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2c87647294b-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the enacted language kept everything but substituted for that italicized language the phrase \"that has\" -- that -- excuse me, \"that establishes or changes a substantive legal standard.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1484",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2c87647294b01e39896ea21e7ce25cdf4078b9f3e1e030772acc2f4712804b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2c87647294b-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So (a)(2) says that any rule, requirement, or other statement of policy that establishes a substantive legal change has to go through informal rulemaking, not even formal rulemaking. And so, really, the question all boils down to what does \"substantive\" mean, I think, as -- as -- as I understand it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1484",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2c87647294b01e39896ea21e7ce25cdf4078b9f3e1e030772acc2f4712804b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2c87647294b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May -- may I take you back, Mr. Kneedler, to one of Justice Sotomayor's original questions, which is just Heritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1484",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2c87647294b01e39896ea21e7ce25cdf4078b9f3e1e030772acc2f4712804b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2c87647294b-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But when is ever a statement of policy binding?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1484",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2c87647294b01e39896ea21e7ce25cdf4078b9f3e1e030772acc2f4712804b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2c87647294b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "By making the legal determination to count Part C days as Part A entitled days in the Medicare fraction, the agency's 2014 issuance reduced the payment right of hospitals nationwide by -- and this is according to the agency's own estimate -- billions of dollars."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1484",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2c87647294b01e39896ea21e7ce25cdf4078b9f3e1e030772acc2f4712804b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2c87647294b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Do you have any other case that that might be when the conference report says we're reflecting recent cases? Is there anything else other than Bowen that you think it might be referring to?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1484",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2c87647294b01e39896ea21e7ce25cdf4078b9f3e1e030772acc2f4712804b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2c87647294b-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: You don't see it or you --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1484",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2c87647294b01e39896ea21e7ce25cdf4078b9f3e1e030772acc2f4712804b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2c87647294b-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: You -- you explained away the last 5,000 pages of the manual."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1484",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2c87647294b01e39896ea21e7ce25cdf4078b9f3e1e030772acc2f4712804b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2c87647294b-0002-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Do you have any idea why this change wasn't put through the ordinary rulemaking notice and --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1484",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2c87647294b01e39896ea21e7ce25cdf4078b9f3e1e030772acc2f4712804b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2c87647294b-0002-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Well, I guess the way the government puts it is they decided not to proceed through rulemaking but to proceed through adjudication."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1484",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2c87647294b01e39896ea21e7ce25cdf4078b9f3e1e030772acc2f4712804b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2c87647294b-0002-0012",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The term \"rule\" in the lead-in to subsection (a)(2) includes statements of policy. So there's some redundancy or some -- it's superfluous there anyway, no matter -- no matter how you read it. So it is -- it is imprecise."
    },
    {
